<title>USA: Danaher buys Asian hand tools business.</title>
<headline>Danaher buys Asian hand tools business.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. tool and component maker Danaher Corp on Thursday said it bought a group of hand tool companies from the Chow family for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>The companies own three factories in China, a distribution center in Taiwan and a new factory and distribution center in Texas.</p>
<p>Danaher said revenues of the acquired firms were about $40 million in 1996 and have been growing at 20 percent a year for several years.  It said the purchase would allow it access to the Asian market and an excellent manufacturing base.  -- New York Newsroom 212 859 1610</p>
</text>
